<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Desperate Hours December, 1985</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;CMO: The Desperate Hours December, 1985&lt;BR&gt;Al “Beirutdude” Sandrik&lt;BR&gt;The Time Is: 2 December, 1985 06:00:00 Zulu/20:00:00 Murmansk Time&lt;BR&gt;AOR: The Norwegian Sea &lt;BR&gt;Playable as NATO only&lt;BR&gt;1 1/2 Day Duration&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;World War Three is entering its third month. Amazingly neither side has yet resorted to nuclear weapons but the balance of power is gradually shifting. Younger members of the Politburo prevented the old guard from implementing the “Seven Days to the Rhine” plan with its first use of over 600 nuclear weapons, arguing the Warsaw Pact’s conventional forces can carry the day. At first all seemed to be going well and by day 14 Soviet troops and their Warsaw Pact allies were on the Rhine in all but southern Bavaria. What the Warsaw Pact planners didn’t count on was full French participation in the NATO defense. Over the next few weeks West German, American, French and Canadian troops stabilized the southern front with UK, Dutch and Belgian forces fighting for the old World War Two battlefields of Arnhem, Essen and Cologne. The once mobile battlefield takes on a World War One trench warfare pattern as PGMs are used up and MBTs/IFVs are destroyed.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;At sea the navies quickly destroy many capital ships and escorts. NATO has largely swept the Warsaw Pact navies from the all but the Soviet home waters, but the fighting was largely Pyrrhic for NATO. The Soviet Northern, Baltic and Black Sea fleets largely have largely ceased to exist. NATOs losses we steep as well with Foch, America, Ark Royal and Saratoga sunk and Invincible, Nimitz and Eisenhower severely damaged.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;The bulk of the NATO navies are now tasked with protecting the NATO North Atlantic Convoys from the remaining Soviet submarines. The reinforcing regular U.S Army Divisions have married up with their equipment in Germany (REFORGER) and the 24th Mech Division has been escorted over by sea. Now American National Guard Divisions and Canadian forces are en route. The Polish and Hungarian forces are becoming restless and the Soviet Category II and III division mobilization is not going well with resistance to the call up. Within weeks NATO will be able to take the offensive surging back into the North German Plain. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;In Moscow, the balance of power is shifting, the ministers who opposed the “Seven Days to the Rhine” plan have now been discredited and the nuclear war hawks have neutralized them. NATO intelligence begins to pick up indications of Soviet preparations for a nuclear strike on the Continental United States (CONUS), Alaska, the UK and France. NATO navies are out of position for this with most forces involved in the Battle of the Atlantic and reinforcing Israel in the Med. USS Pharris FF-1094, charged with defending the GIUK Gap, and a few P-3s are all that stands between a Soviet Yankee reinforcing Soviet nuclear forces in the Atlantic and maybe the tipping point in the balance to nuclear war.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;1. This is a very simple scenario, I really designed it to test out some Lua scripting. &lt;BR&gt;Make sure you have the message window set to pop up&lt;BR&gt;2. A gale center will move across the patrol area with increasing winds and sea and higher ambient noise in the water column. (weather Lua scripting). Watch the weather forecasts and weather observations. &lt;BR&gt;3. Your P-3B/Cs will do a system check every five (5) minutes and have a two (2)&amp;nbsp;percent chance of having to RTB due to a systems failure (other Lua scripting). &lt;BR&gt;4. The aircraft operations are set to Sustained due to the later stage in the war, please do not change to Surge.&lt;BR&gt;5. The commercial shipping represents neutrals and fishing boats from Norway/Iceland. This far into the war, there will be some shipping returning to the seas, and people have to eat.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1.01 Build 1143.1 – Data Base: DB3000 483&lt;BR&gt;An .INI and Delta File have both been provided for rebuilds&lt;BR&gt;Al “BeirutDude” Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;BR&gt;&lt;A href="mailto:Al.Sandrik@gmail.com"&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
